                                                                        <tr>
                                                                            <th>Brief Profile:</th>
                                                                            <td><p>Prof. Nisha Varghese is currently Director of the School of Extension and Development Studies at Indira Gandhi National Open University, New Delhi. A merit holder during Graduation and a gold medalist during her Master&rsquo;s programme, she attained her Doctoral degree in Agricultural Economics from the University of Agricultural Sciences, Dharwad, Karnataka, India. Her areas of teaching and research interest are Quantitative Techniques, Research Methods, Desertification, Labour Migration, Agriculture and other Development related issues.</p>
<p>She has professional experience in various organizations of repute like Agricultural Finance Corporation (AFC), Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), Institute of Economic Growth (IEG) and National Centre for Agricultural Economics and Policy Research (NCAP). Prof. Varghese joined IGNOU in 2009 and since then she has been associated with various activities like teaching, preparation of self learning materials, radio counseling, teleconferencing, Programme Design and Development etc.. She has guided students for their Dissertation in MA in Extension and Development Studies and has also guided PhD students. She has also been a member of the Academic Council Standing Committee and Academic Council of IGNOU and School Board member of four different Schools of Study at IGNOU. While at IGNOU, she has presented papers in several international conferences. She has served as channel coordinator of Swayam Prabha Channel 13 on Professional Education. Prof. Varghese has an edited book published by Springer Nature and an authored book by Routledge to her credit other than several publications in various national and international journals and books.She is also a member of the editorial board of Indian Journal of Open Learning published by IGNOU.</p>
<p>Currently she is coordinating Post Graduate Diploma in Corporate Social Responsibility (PGDCSR) and MA in Corporate Social Responsibility (MACSR) programmes offered by the School of Extension and Development Studies.</p>
