                                                                            <th>Brief Profile:</th>
                                                                            <td><p><strong>Dr. SARDA PRASAD</strong></p>
<p>Dr. Sarda Prasad is working as Assistant Professor in School of Extension and Development Studies, IGNOU since 2021. He has MPhil and PhD in Population Studies from Centre for the Study of Regional Development (CSRD), Jawaharlal Nehru University (JNU), New Delhi. M.Sc. in Extension Education from Punjab Agricultural University, Ludhiana, Punjab and B.Sc. Agri. (Hons.) from CS Azad University of Agriculture and Technology, Kanpur, UP. He has bagged MA in Economics from Bundelkhand University, Jhansi, MA in Distance Education, Post Graduate Diploma in Rural Development, Post Graduate Diploma in Distance Education, Post Graduate Diploma in Women and Gender Studies, Appreciation Course on Population and Sustainable Development, Certificate on Life and Thought of B.R. Ambedkar, and Certificate on Visual Arts (painting) from IGNOU.</p>
<p>He has awarded <strong>Gold Medal</strong> for Post Graduate Diploma in Rural Development (PGDRD), IGNOU, 2020; Awarded &ldquo;Best Oral Presentation Award&rdquo; for the paper entitled &ldquo;Demographic Study of Agrarian Society for Sustainable Development&rdquo; presented at International Extension Education Conference on &ldquo;Education, Research and Services&rdquo; organized by Department of Extension Education, Institute of Agricultural Sciences, Banaras Hindu University (BHU), Varanasi (UP), Awarded ICSSR Travel grant (full funding) for participation and oral presentation of paper in the International Conference, held at Beijing, China. He has cleared ICAR-Junior Research Fellowship (JRF), UGC-NET-JRF and SRF in Adult Education (2005) &amp;UGC-NET-JRF in Population Studies (2009) &amp; ICAR-ASRB-NET in Agricultural Extension (2011).</p>
<p>Prior to joining IGNOU, he has worked Research Associate, Census Data Manager, Data Analyst in various organization. He has more than nine years of teaching, research and extension activities. He has worked as Post Doctoral Fellow (PDF) at CSRD, JNU. His academic interest on Population Studies (Migration, Morbidity and Mortality), Agriculture and Rural Development, Extension and Development Studies, Gender Studies, Distance Education, Urban, and Tribal Studies.</p>
<p>He has published 5 articles in International Refereed Journal; 14 articles in National refereed Journals; Major Reports (Co-author), 2 popular articles in Newspapers; 7 reference books, 11 book chapters, 41 units for self learning material (IGNOU) and Reviewed 52 articles those published in ICSSR Journal of Abstracts and Reviews &ndash; Economics. He is a life member of 6 academic bodies such ISLE, IASP, IASSH, SEEA, ISS, ISEE.</p>
<p>Currently he is coordinating 3 programmes PG Diploma in Population and Family Health Studies (PGDPFHS), PG Diploma in Tribal Studies (PGDTRBS), MA in Population and Family Health Studies (MAPFHS) offered by SOEDS, and coordinating 7 Courses of the programmes.&nbsp;</p>
